Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* feat(desktop): paint the sidebar from the stored session outcome [daveey]

- sessionStatusStripe: row.outcome wins when present (done green, decision red,
  muted grey, waiting/running grey glyph, unresolved amber); a live turn and a
  ⌘B park still beat it; no outcome keeps the old derivation.
- Stripe tooltip from the outcome: summary, open questions, what it waits on,
  or the unresolved reason in words.
- ⌘B writes through POST /api/sessions/{id}/mute and reads row.muted; the
  local list stays as the optimistic cache and as the only record against an
  older backend. A failed POST reverts and toasts.
- kanban_notice rows with display_metadata.stale render dimmed, labelled
  "outdated: card moved on".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* feat(desktop): push old local ⌘B parks to the backend once [daveey]

The first sidebar page whose rows carry `muted` POSTs /mute {muted: true} for
every locally parked row the backend reports unmuted, then records the profile
(per gateway) so it never runs again. A 404 leaves the local list alone; other
failures retry on the next load.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix(desktop): unmute clears the stale muted outcome; bots ignore outcomes [daveey]

- A ⌘B write updates the row's outcome with `muted`: muting stamps a `muted`
  outcome, unmuting drops one, so the stripe falls back to the derived logic
  until the next list page instead of staying grey.
- Automated rows resurface only on the signals they always did; a stored
  outcome (e.g. unresolved → amber) no longer pulls bot traffic back in.
- The list identity gate compares `muted` and `outcome`, so a page that moves
  only those lands.
- Tests: the sidebar refresh runs the migration (fails if the call is
  removed), setSessionMutedRemote's real path/body through the request helper,
  the unmute/mute row update, automated rows with outcomes, the identity gate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix(kanban): sync diff ignores other gateways' chat links on picked-up foreign cards [daveey]

A copy of another gateway's card (kanban_worker_node.import_cards) carries runs, comments, attachments and
events but no chat links; the creator's chats are read from the replica. diff() still compared every
task_chat_links row of a live card against the replica, so each running foreign copy was a permanent
child_mismatch with pending=0 (hub, 2026-10-29: t_01a1895c0a80c903 macbook/created). Links of this gateway's
own chats on those cards, and every link on own cards, are still compared.

Kanban: t_01a1895d106aeb02

* refactor(desktop): bring session-outcome under the code-health caps [daveey]

- Stripe hook + component move to sidebar/session-row-stripe.tsx (one
  component for the bar and the glyph); session-row shrinks.
- derivedStatusStripe split into isStuck / parkedStripe / settledStripe.
- Outcome types move to types/session-outcome.ts; row status copy (kanban,
  process badges, outcome tooltips) moves to i18n/en_session_row_status.ts
  and types_session_row_status.ts, unresolved reasons as a table.
- Stale-notice spreads and the list signature's status stamps become helpers;
  committedDuringTurn moves to its own module to offset utils.ts.

No behaviour change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix(ci): ci-flaky-cards defers to the card core's create_overlap guard names instead of crashing on its exit-2 stdout refusal

* test(tui_gateway): deflake hosted room service waits (2s/5s fixed deadlines -> 30s event-style waits)

* fix(kanban): a dry-run dispatch writes no suspend-ledger stamp [daveey]

bc67ee012f stamps kanban_dispatch_stamp on every reclaim phase, including
dispatch_once(dry_run=True), so dry runs created two tables in kanban.db and
four 'dry run changes nothing' tests went red on main (test_kanban_refused_pin_clear,
_managed_pin_policy, _model_assignment). A dry-run stamp would also hide a real
suspend gap from the next pass. record_dispatch_pass(dry_run=True) is a no-op;
the reclaim phase passes dispatch_once's dry_run through.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix(sessions): CLI and web outcome refresh load plugin providers and judge first [daveey]

Without plugins loaded, `hermes sessions outcome-audit --refresh` (run by the
auditor cron every 10 min) re-derived without the user-steps provider and
stored `done` over chats waiting on a user decision.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* test(cron): synchronize terminal fire-fence revocation [daveey]

* fix(ci): dry-run dispatch writes nothing; GET /api/sessions draft sweep opens writable only with drafts to archive [daveey]

bc67ee012ff stamped kanban.db on dry-run ticks (skip _record_dispatch_pass when dry_run);
851e72eed44 made every session-list poll open state.db writable and stamp last_draft_archive
(probe read-only, stamp only after archiving); the gateway-lock test fake lacked the new method.
Supersedes #226.

* fix(kanban): sync diff ignores other gateways' chat links on picked-up foreign cards [daveey]

A copy of another gateway's card (kanban_worker_node.import_cards) carries runs, comments, attachments and
events but no chat links; the creator's chats are read from the replica. diff() still compared every
task_chat_links row of a live card against the replica, so each running foreign copy was a permanent
child_mismatch with pending=0 (hub, 2026-10-29: t_01a1895c0a80c903 macbook/created). Links of this gateway's
own chats on those cards, and every link on own cards, are still compared.

Kanban: t_01a1895d106aeb02

